# Rover 800 four-door saloon, 1986-1999.
#
# GRAPHICS REPLACED 2026-11-17. These four objects keep their names, dates and
# weights so that savegames stay valid, but their sprites now show the XX of
# 1986-91 rather than a generic 1986-99 shell. The facelift R17 of 1991-99 is a
# separate set of objects (Rover800R17), so the two marks appear side by side on
# the road, as they did. The XX master is citycars/4.5/rover-800-xx.blend.
#
# The Rover 800, developed with Honda (the Legend twin): 4,690 mm long, 1,730 mm
# wide, 1,400 mm high, 2,760 mm wheelbase; 2.0 fours, 2.7 Honda V6 then Rover's
# own 2.5/2.7 KV6, 820 and Sterling trims. Facelift in 1991 and again in 1996.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_800
#
# Colours: Nightfire Red, Charcoal Grey, White Gold and Steel Blue are documented
# Rover finishes of the period.
#
# Weight: 100 in total (red 30, grey 26, white 24, blue 20).
#
# Speed 210 km/h; comfort 110/495 (line). Classes 2,3.
# Dates: 1986-1999 with a road tail to about 2010.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-800.blend. References:
# citycars/references/rover-800/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=Rover800(NightfireRed)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=30
intro_year=1986
intro_month=7
retire_year=2010
retire_month=6
speed=210
length=3
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=110
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=495

Image[E]=./images/rover-800-red_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/rover-800-red_SE.0.0,-13,0
